# 15. Create a Disease Detection App with Gradio

Install Gradio if necessary:

```python
!pip install -q gradio
```

Then create the application:

```python
import gradio as gr
import numpy as np
import tensorflow as tf
import json

# Load model
model = tf.keras.models.load_model(
    "/content/best_mango_model.keras"
)

# Load class names
with open("/content/class_names.json", "r") as f:
    class_names = json.load(f)


def predict_mango_disease(image):

    # Resize image
    image = image.resize((224, 224))

    # Convert to NumPy array
    image_array = np.array(image)

    # Remove alpha channel if present
    if image_array.shape[-1] == 4:
        image_array = image_array[:, :, :3]

    # Add batch dimension
    image_array = np.expand_dims(image_array, axis=0)

    # Prediction
    predictions = model.predict(
        image_array,
        verbose=0
    )[0]

    # Return class probabilities
    results = {
        class_names[i]: float(predictions[i])
        for i in range(len(class_names))
    }

    return results
```

---

# 16. Launch the Web App

```python
demo = gr.Interface(
    fn=predict_mango_disease,

    inputs=gr.Image(
        type="pil",
        label="Upload Mango Leaf Image"
    ),

    outputs=gr.Label(
        num_top_classes=3,
        label="Prediction"
    ),

    title="🥭 Mango Leaf Disease Detection",

    description="""
Upload an image of a mango leaf.

The AI model will classify it into one of the following categories:

• Anthracnose
• Bacterial Canker
• Cutting Weevil
• Die Back
• Gall Midge
• Healthy
• Powdery Mildew
• Sooty Mould
"""
)

demo.launch(share=True)
```

After running this cell in Colab, Gradio will provide a link where you can:

1. Upload a mango leaf image.
2. The image is resized to `224 × 224`.
3. MobileNetV2 processes the image.
4. The model predicts the disease.
5. The app displays the **top 3 predicted classes with confidence scores**.

