After training, you will have:

```text
/content/
│
├── dataset/
│   └── MangoLeafBD Dataset/
│       ├── Anthracnose/
│       ├── Bacterial Canker/
│       ├── Cutting Weevil/
│       ├── Die Back/
│       ├── Gall Midge/
│       ├── Healthy/
│       ├── Powdery Mildew/
│       └── Sooty Mould/
│
├── best_mango_model.keras
│
└── class_names.json
```

### Optional: Download the trained model

```python
from google.colab import files

files.download("/content/best_mango_model.keras")
files.download("/content/class_names.json")
```

One important improvement I recommend before considering the reported accuracy final: use a **stratified image-level split** rather than splitting batched datasets, so the validation and test sets are precisely separated and each of your 8 classes remains balanced.
